  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${g}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{1}{t}-t,\\,2\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}-t)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-2+{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+2+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}+t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061e+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2})-(\\operatorname{ln}\u20611+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
